\subsection{Specificity Control: Top-24 vs.\ Bottom-24 Head Ablation}
\label{sec:specificity_control}

To test whether ablation effects are specific to instruction-dominant heads, we compare ablating the top-24 heads (highest instruction attention fraction, i.e., the instruction-dominant group) against the bottom-24 heads (lowest instruction attention fraction).
The two groups overlap on 16 heads and differ only on the top-8 vs.\ bottom-8 extremes.

